        "width" : 0,
        "title" : null,
        "hasTitle" : false,
        "message" : [
          "***Goal***\r",
          "\r",
          "After running `ctgan_augment_bank_transfers.py`, this notebook validates the CTGAN-generated synthetic transfers and prepares an augmented transaction data set and property graph for further analysis.\r",
          "\r",
          "For graph algorithms, metrics, and OML K-Means clustering before creation of `BANK_ACCOUNTS_CLUSTERED_V`, see the separate Graph Algorithms and OML notebooks.\r",
          "\r",
          "**You will learn how to:**\r",
          "\r",
          "1- Validate synthetic transfers and review their source and destination account-holder names.\r",
          "\r",
          "2- Verify foreign-key constraints and account references.\r",
          "\r",
          "3- Create `BANK_TRANSFERS_AUGMENTED` by combining original and synthetic transfers.\r",
          "\r",
          "4- Create and verify the `BANK_GRAPH_AUGMENTED` property graph.\r",
          "\r",
          "5- Compute and save PageRank, betweenness, closeness, and 2-, 3-, and 4-hop cycle metrics using SQL Property Graph and PGX Python.\r",
          "\r",
          "6- Merge and Normalize metrics between 0 and 100\r",
          "\r",
          "7- After running the OML Graph Algorithms notebook, create\r",
          "\r",
          " a- `BANK_ACCOUNTS_CLUSTERED_V` and the enriched\r",
          "\r",
          "b-`BANK_GRAPH_AUGMENTED_CLUSTER` property graph with graph metrics and cluster IDs."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "html",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : true,
        "hideResult" : false,
        "hideGutter" : true,
        "hideVizConfig" : false,
        "hideInIFrame" : false,
        "enabled" : true,
        "forms" : "[]",
        "result" : {
          "startTime" : 1787917027501,
          "endTime" : 1787917027534,
          "interpreter" : "md",
          "taskStatus" : "SUCCESS",
          "status" : "SUCCESS",
          "results" : [
            {
              "message" : "<p><em><strong>Goal</strong></em></p>\n<p>After running <code>ctgan_augment_bank_transfers.py</code>, this notebook validates the CTGAN-generated synthetic transfers and prepares an augmented transaction data set and property graph for further analysis.</p>\n<p>For graph algorithms, metrics, and OML K-Means clustering before creation of <code>BANK_ACCOUNTS_CLUSTERED_V</code>, see the separate Graph Algorithms and OML notebooks.</p>\n<p><strong>You will learn how to:</strong></p>\n<p>1- Validate synthetic transfers and review their source and destination account-holder names.</p>\n<p>2- Verify foreign-key constraints and account references.</p>\n<p>3- Create <code>BANK_TRANSFERS_AUGMENTED</code> by combining original and synthetic transfers.</p>\n<p>4- Create and verify the <code>BANK_GRAPH_AUGMENTED</code> property graph.</p>\n<p>5- Compute and save PageRank, betweenness, closeness, and 2-, 3-, and 4-hop cycle metrics using SQL Property Graph and PGX Python.</p>\n<p>6- Merge and Normalize metrics between 0 and 100</p>\n<p>7- After running the OML Graph Algorithms notebook, create</p>\n<p>a- <code>BANK_ACCOUNTS_CLUSTERED_V</code> and the enriched</p>\n<p>b-<code>BANK_GRAPH_AUGMENTED_CLUSTER</code> property graph with graph metrics and cluster IDs.</p>\n",
              "type" : "HTML"
            }
          ],
          "forms" : "[]"
        },
        "relations" : [ ],
        "dynamicFormParams" : "{}"
      },
